    48	Re-derivation. Let `F=(P,Q)` be a residual Keller map with geometric degree
    49	`N=4`, and let `T_k(u,v)=(u,v+u^k)`. Then
    50	`F_k=T_k o F=(P,Q+P^k)` is again Keller because `det dT_k=1`, and
    51	`C(P,Q+P^k)=C(P,Q)`, so the function-field degree is still `4`.
    52	Properness is target-isomorphism invariant:
    53	`A_{F_k}=T_k(A_F)`. The finite normal cover can be replaced by
    54	`T_k o q:Y -> A^2`; connectedness, degree, branch locus, local fibre
    55	cardinalities, `a_D`, `a_p`, monodromy classes, normalisations, and incidences
    56	are all pulled through the target isomorphism. Thus `Br=D_1`, `D_0`
    57	unbranched, transposition meridians, disjoint local transpositions at
    58	`Sing D_1`, and the two-component residual structure are preserved.
